<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>AAPSBuildType</key>
	<string>$(CONFIGURATION)</string>
	<key>CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>AAPS talks to your Omnipod DASH pod and Dexcom G7 / ONE+ sensor over Bluetooth, and a RileyLink or OrangeLink can wake it about once a minute in the background to load from Nightscout and check the alarms.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>AAPS uses the camera only to read the set-up QR code shown by your master phone.</string>
	<key>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</key>
	<string>AAPS uses Face ID only to unlock the app and its protected settings, when you have switched that protection on.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>AAPS uses your location only to evaluate automation rules you set up yourself, such as starting a temporary target when you arrive somewhere.</string>
	<!--
	  Lets the app keep running in the background while it plays audio. `IosBackgroundKeepAlive` plays
	  silent sound for this (the LoopFollow way), so the Nightscout connection is not suspended a few
	  seconds after the app leaves the screen. The user can turn it off: Alerts > Keep running in
	  background. Apple does not accept this in the App Store; TestFlight internal testing is fine.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
		<string>bluetooth-central</string>
	</array>
	<!--
	  RileyLink heartbeat (2026-10-23): `IosRileyLinkHeartbeat` connects to a RileyLink or OrangeLink, whose timer tick wakes
	  the app about once a minute in the background. `bluetooth-central` above allows that wake-up. Setting: Alerts >
	  RileyLink heartbeat. This text is what iOS shows when it asks for Bluetooth.
	-->
	<!--
	  BG Live Activity (2026-10-24): lock screen, Dynamic Island, Apple Watch Smart Stack and CarPlay. Drawn by the
	  LiveActivity extension, fed by `SwiftLiveActivity`. The user can turn it off in iPhone Settings for this app.
	-->
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
	<true/>
	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
